Version 1.1.8-b.28

  * The repository is restarted as the launcher and launcher-tests
    packages. The contributors of the earlier history are credited in
    AUTHORS.

  * Log messages issued during exit reach the log file.

  * Path canonicalization errors name the offending path.

  * The --build2-metadata option takes its argument, as build2 expects.

  * HTTP requests that follow a 303 See Other redirect drop the body
    headers of the original request.

  * Replacing a cached file record also replaces its component.

  * The indeterminate progress bar fits the terminal width.

  * The Steam library artwork of IW4x (mm) is tagged MM and the artwork of
    IW4x carries no tag, matching the client names.

  * The Linux launcher runs on glibc 2.36 (Debian 12) and later. It links
    the C++ runtime and its dependencies statically, so it only requires
    glibc from the host.

  * The launcher takes over the DLC files that earlier launchers installed
    into zone/dlc/. The client moved them over the current copies at every
    start, so each update downloaded them again. If such a file cannot be
    moved or removed (e.g., zone/dlc/ is read-only), then the update fails
    with an error that names it, since the client would refuse to start.

  * The launcher starts an installed client while GitHub or the IW4x CDN is
    unavailable. It warns about each component that it could not update
    and only fails if the selected client requires one that is not
    installed. With --skip-launch any failed update is an error.

  * Launches that restart Steam no longer stall for minutes on Linux. The
    Steam processes that the launcher started remained its zombies once
    they exited, which Companion took for a running client and waited for.
